00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.210
You won't catch me.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:53.790
Boo...

00:20:54.830 --> 00:21:00.840
I think you can actually practice casting
with that yarn and rod there. Wanna try?

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:01.920
Yeah!

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:05.840
Okay, sit with the side you're going
to hold the rod towards the wall.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:07.180
Like this?

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:09.350
Start waving like you're
going along the wall.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:11.850
Along the wall...

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.860
It felt like I managed
to cast that straight!

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:21.940
In order to make a nice, straight loop,
you need to wave the rod straight, too.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:23.030
Huh...

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.910
So if you practice using the wall,

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:29.620
you'll be able to cast
straight out on the water, too.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.830
Ooh, I see!

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:34.330
You're waving it around too much!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:36.420
In order to avoid that,

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:41.250
try to imagine the angle from
11 o'clock to 1 o'clock on a clock.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:47.140
To cast forward, try to stop
your rod at 11 for two seconds.

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:51.140
And when you back cast, you stop at 1.

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:54.810
The line that's moving straight and faster

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:58.190
will be affected by the
rod's resistance when it stops and...

00:21:58.190 --> 00:22:00.770
You'll be able to make a pretty loop.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:09.700
Wow... I feel like the yarn
moved the way I wanted it to.

00:22:11.030 --> 00:22:14.620
I wanna go fishing as soon as possible!

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:20.040
Aren't you embarrassed to
be fishing when you're a girl?

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:24.460
I wonder why Futaba asked me that.

00:22:30.180 --> 00:22:32.760
